WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.664
Roadmap step three: draft a one-line offer they can understand in one breath.

00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:07.534
This lesson is about draft a one-line offer.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:08.610
Roadmap step 3.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.122
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:14.710
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:20.091
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:24.038
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:27.984
Stay practical: write one-line offer before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.304 --> 00:00:32.659
Write: who it is for, what changes, and how they get it.

00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:34.836
Remember the objective: write one-line offer.

00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:38.828
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.828 --> 00:00:43.182
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:47.174
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:51.528
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.528 --> 00:00:54.068
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.068 --> 00:00:55.520
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.606
Cut adjectives.

00:00:56.606 --> 00:00:59.287
Keep the promise and the delivery path.

